<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:orc="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:dev="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:vc="clr-namespace:CoenQcCalibrateValve;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>Delivers water on one valve at a reward's pulse width (Pip, 11 Nov 2026), so a valve's calibration can be checked by weighing what it gives: Pulses pulses of PulseWidthMs on Channel at PulseGapMs, fired on the board's Harp clock as the calibration fires them (OpenRigs.Core FirePulses). rig-control's Calibrations page works out the width and the pulses from the valve's curve (1 ml at the reward size) and gives the curve's pulseGapMs; the board's port, its RewardValve lines and the lick spout stage come from this machine's rig.yml, read into the lab rig model (OpenRigs.Devices ReadLabRig). The hardware is the lab's device pieces, as in a session (OpenRigs.Devices ReadyGate, BehaviorBoard, ClockFromBoard, PulseOutputs, LickSpoutStage); a delivery has no experiment folder (OpenRigs.Logging NoExperimentFolder), so no piece logs. On a rig with a lick spout stage the spouts go to rig.yml's lickSpoutDefaultPosition first and out after (Extensions\Spouts.bonsai). Ready once the board's clock is set, its pulse setup has gone out and the spouts are in; Go fires the pulses, reporting each as the delivered metric; Finished once the last has closed. Nothing is written.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="ConfigRoot" DisplayName="ConfigRoot" Description="The root under which each machine has its own configuration directory, &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;MACHINE-NAME&gt;\rig.yml." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Settings</Name>
        <Description>RigConfigDirectory is &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;MACHINE-NAME&gt;; RigConfigs is rig.yml there in the lab rig model (OpenRigs.Devices ReadLabRig, as every lab workflow reads it). RewardValveLines is the lines BehaviorBoard-Main's wiring gives a RewardValve (OpenRigs.Devices WiredOutputs); it stops the workflow if rig.yml has no such board or no RewardValve on DO1 to DO3. NoExperimentFolder (OpenRigs.Logging) declares PathPrefix, never published, as a delivery has no experiment folder, so the pieces' logs, which wait for it, never start; and SubjectId, _valve-calibration_, no mouse's, so the spouts go to rig.yml's lickSpoutDefaultPosition.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="ConfigRoot" DisplayName="ConfigRoot" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadLabRig.bonsai">
              <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:WiredOutputs">
                <dev:Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</dev:Board>
                <dev:Device>RewardValve</dev:Device>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>RewardValveLines</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Boolean">
              <rx:Name>SpoutsReady</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:NoExperimentFolder.bonsai">
              <SubjectId>_valve-calibration_</SubjectId>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" />
        <Property Name="SessionId" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl) over TCP 5561, which the rig agent relays. Reports Recording at Go.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SubjectId" />
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <SessionId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
              <Parameters>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>SpoutStepSize</Name>
                  <Value />
                  <Description>Motor steps each spout nudge moves, taken live by the lick spout stage (OpenRigs.Devices LickSpoutStage, on a rig with one). A delivery sends no nudge; the stage shows its default here at Start.</Description>
                  <Minimum>1</Minimum>
                  <WholeNumber>true</WholeNumber>
                </Parameter>
              </Parameters>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Recording</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Hardware</Name>
        <Description>The rig's pieces, as in a session (lib-open-rigs building-blocks): the Ready gate (ReadyGate), the behavior board BehaviorBoard-Main on rig.yml's port (BehaviorBoard, which clears any ZapitTrigger line however the workflow stops), its clock (ClockFromBoard: Timestamp, the board's own time from its analog data events, 1 kHz, which the pulses are timed on, as before the device pieces) and its pulsed lines (PulseOutputs: rig.yml's outputPulseEnable without the ZapitTrigger line, stopping at Start if a RewardValve line is not among them; TriggerCalibratedPulse fires one pulse of a given width on a line). Ready (ReadyGate) once the clock is set and DeliveryReady has come: 1 s after the board's first event, once PulseOutputs' setup has gone out, and once the spouts are in (SpoutsReady).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadyGate.bonsai">
              <ReadyWaitsFor>HarpClockSet, DeliveryReady</ReadyWaitsFor>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.BehaviorBoard.bonsai">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
              <CommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</CommandsSubjectName>
              <DataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</DataSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.ClockFromBoard.bonsai">
              <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
              <BoardDataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BoardDataSubjectName>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.PulseOutputs.bonsai">
              <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
              <BoardDataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BoardDataSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Delay">
                <rx:DueTime>PT1S</rx:DueTime>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>SpoutsReady</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orc:AnnounceStage">
                <orc:Stage>DeliveryReady</orc:Stage>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>ReadyStages</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Channel" DisplayName="Channel" Description="The valve's behavior board line, 1 to 3 (DO1 to DO3): a RewardValve in rig.yml's wiring. rig-control gives it at launch." />
        <Property Name="PulseWidthMs" DisplayName="PulseWidthMs" Description="Each pulse's width in ms: the reward size's, read off the valve's curve by rig-control." />
        <Property Name="Pulses" DisplayName="Pulses" Description="How many pulses: 1 ml at the reward size, by rig-control." />
        <Property Name="PulseGapMs" DisplayName="PulseGapMs" Description="The off-to-on time between pulses, in ms: the valve calibration file's pulseGapMs, which rig-control gives at launch." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Deliver</Name>
        <Description>At Go, Pulses pulses of PulseWidthMs on Channel at PulseGapMs through TriggerCalibratedPulse (DeliverTrain, src\Extensions, into OpenRigs.Core FirePulses on the Harp clock), each reported as the delivered metric (how many so far); once the last has closed, Finished, and Delivered ends, which takes the spouts out. Stops the workflow if Channel is not a RewardValve in rig.yml.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Channel" />
              <Property Name="PulseWidthMs" />
              <Property Name="Pulses" />
              <Property Name="PulseGapMs" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RewardValveLines</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="vc:DeliverTrain">
                <vc:Channel>1</vc:Channel>
                <vc:PulseWidthMs>1</vc:PulseWidthMs>
                <vc:Pulses>0</vc:Pulses>
                <vc:PulseGapMs>0</vc:PulseGapMs>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="Line" Selector="Line" />
                <Property Name="PulseWidthMs" Selector="PulseWidthMs" />
                <Property Name="Pulses" Selector="Pulses" />
                <Property Name="PulseGapMs" Selector="PulseGapMs" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orc:FirePulses">
                <orc:Line>1</orc:Line>
                <orc:PulseWidthMs>1</orc:PulseWidthMs>
                <orc:Pulses>0</orc:Pulses>
                <orc:PulseGapMs>0</orc:PulseGapMs>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>TriggerCalibratedPulse</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:ElementIndex" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>it.Index + 1</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>delivered</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Last" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Finished</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject">
              <Name>Delivered</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="Extensions\Spouts.bonsai">
        <SpoutsForwardSteps>0</SpoutsForwardSteps>
        <DoneSubjectName>Delivered</DoneSubjectName>
        <DoneCommand>SpoutsOut</DoneCommand>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
